cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OreSecStitch in your work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "OreSecStitch: Reconstruction of closed triangulated surfaces from planar geological contour stacks"
abstract: >-
  OreSecStitch reconstructs a closed triangulated surface from a stack of planar
  contours, such as geological cross-sections of an orebody. It provides a
  Python API, contour loaders, geometry metrics, and a configurable experiment
  driver, together with two example contour datasets.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "OreSecStitch authors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
license: "GPL-3.0-only"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CloudComputer/OreSecStitch"
url: "https://github.com/CloudComputer/OreSecStitch"
keywords:
  - geological modeling
  - contour stitching
  - surface reconstruction
  - orebody
  - triangulation
  - computational geometry
